.DS_Store
# K6 fix: was a bare `qa/` (directory-pattern, unanchored — matches a qa/ dir at ANY depth). Git's
# own rule is "it is not possible to re-include a file if a parent directory of that file is
# excluded", so EVERY negation below (and every demo's own `!qa/gate_skips.jsonl` in its local
# .gitignore, meant to be committed per AGENTS.md/the design doc) was silently defeated by this one
# line, with git giving no warning either way. `**/qa/*` keeps the same "ignore everything under any
# qa/ dir by default, at any depth" effect while actually letting a later, more specific `!qa/<file>`
# (root- or demo-local) win — a plain `qa/*` would NOT do this: a pattern with a slash in the middle
# is anchored to the .gitignore's OWN directory (root here), so it would silently stop matching any
# demos/*/qa/ path at all.
**/qa/*
public/fonts/
fonts.lock.json
# ...except the font-coverage gate's own good/bad fixtures — those MUST be tracked so a fresh clone
# (not just this working tree) actually exercises the gate; the bare pattern above was silently
# hiding them from git, which made bad/ fall through to a false "no lock file, SKIP" exit 0 in any
# clone (see scripts/run-fixture-tests.mjs's font-coverage suite, and the 2026-09 publish review).
!packages/kit/gates/__fixtures__/font-coverage/**/fonts.lock.json
# demos/explainer's own qa/font-size-check.config.json (which on-screen caption region to measure —
# authored PROJECT CONFIG, not a build artifact) is un-ignored in that demo's OWN .gitignore, not
# here: a demo-local .gitignore is read AFTER this one and wins for paths under it, so a root-level
# negation for a demo-local file would be silently overridden by that demo's own `qa/*.json` rule.
